{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## HYPOTHESIS REJECTED — this is NOT a budget defect. Returning to Phase 1.\n\nThe 1800s verification run **30978613228** (branch scratch-941b-probe, commit c89cabf9c9)\nALSO expired, and the way it expired refutes the budget hypothesis rather than merely failing\nto confirm it:\n\n    RuntimeError: ... still absent after 181 poll(s) over 1800s.\n    Last observation: GET /rest/api/2/field -> HTTP 200, 27 field(s); names observed:\n    ['Archived', 'Archiver', 'Attachment', ... 'Σ Time Spent']\n\n**The inventory is byte-identical to the 600s failure.** Same 27 names, same zero\n`customfield_*`, three times the wait. A plugin mid-registration progresses; this did not move\nat all.\n\n**The container log settles it.** From the run's own `docker compose logs`:\n\n    2026-08-05 05:40:58 [c.a.jira.startup.LauncherContextListener] Startup is complete.\n                        Jira is ready to serve.\n    2026-08-05 05:41:53 [c.a.jira.upgrade.UpgradeScheduler] Plugins upgrades completed\n                        successfully\n    (last container line: 05:41:57)\n\nThe wait then failed at **06:11:19**. Jira had been fully started, with plugin upgrades\nCOMPLETE, and the container completely silent, for **~29 minutes**. There is no registration\nstill in flight to wait for. **No budget fixes this.** The decision rule 9790 wrote — 'no\n`customfield_*` at all ⇒ the plugin is still starting ⇒ the budget is too short' — is itself\nwrong for this instance, and it is what pointed both 9790 and this ticket's original diagnosis\nat the budget.\n\n## New leading hypothesis — an ORDERING DEADLOCK, not a timing shortfall\n\n`Epic Link`/`Epic Name` are provisioned by GreenHopper when the first Jira **Software**\nproject is created — not at plugin startup. The harness creates its scratch projects from the\npinned template `com.pyxis.greenhopper.jira:gh-scrum-template`\n(`conftest.py:447`, `_create_scratch_project`). So 9790's session-start gate waits for a\ncapability that only exists after an action the gate itself blocks.\n\nThat explains EVERY symptom with one cause:\n- run 30964805133 green pre-1406: no gate, suite created projects, fields appeared, and\n  `_assert_project_capabilities` — which runs AFTER creation — passed.\n- runs 30975323866 (600s) and 30978613228 (1800s) red: budget-independent, because the\n  precondition is an action, not elapsed time.\n- both probe runs (30944211742, 30930839323) red the same way: the probe also waits before it\n  creates anything.\n- the identical inventory and the idle container.\n\n## Discriminating experiment now running: 30981084637\n\nDispatched on the epic-link probe workflow (~15 min, not the ~50-min harness) with the probe\nstep replaced by: snapshot the field inventory -> wait 180s QUIET with no project ->\nsnapshot again -> create the pinned GreenHopper scrum project -> poll the inventory.\n\n- If the ordering hypothesis is TRUE: absent before, still absent after the quiet 180s, and\n  present within seconds of the project create.\n- If FALSE (genuine degrade): absent in all three, which would also contradict the green run\n  and send the investigation at the image instead.\n\nThe quiet-settle leg is what discriminates 'needs an action' from 'needs more time' — it gives\ntime WITHOUT the action.\n\n**No fix will be pushed until this returns.** The previous diagnosis looked airtight and cost a\n50-minute run; the corrected one gets an experiment designed to falsify it, not to agree."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785910928745271001,"uuid":"0908161d-c2bb-46ea-a98e-5980f5326aca"}